    {
      "id": "G5HQkwSvgdSrAizWN425o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1871.354089125902,
      "y": 1157.5030898448563,
      "width": 1576.0789794921875,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0V",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 565945022,
      "version": 24,
      "versionNonce": 2049411490,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1784224564459,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Network Manager manages all API requests and streaming connections. \nThis module abstracts away the details of HTTP requests and Server-Sent Events (SSE), so the rest of the app doesn’t have to worry about transport logic. \nIt also centralizes error handling, retries, and analytics tracking, ensuring a consistent user experience.\n\nNetwork Manager: Handles:\n-- Fetching conversation lists and message history\n-- Sending user prompts to the backend\n-- Receiving streamed responses from the server\n-- Managing auth headers and API tokens\n-- Tracking performance, errors, and user analytics\nState management is handled through a central store, using either React Context, Redux, or Zustand. \nThis global state holds conversation threads, user metadata, loading and error states, and UI preferences. \nIt enables any component to react to updates and keeps the UI in sync with the backend",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A Network Manager manages all API requests and streaming connections. \nThis module abstracts away the details of HTTP requests and Server-Sent Events (SSE), so the rest of the app doesn’t have to worry about transport logic. \nIt also centralizes error handling, retries, and analytics tracking, ensuring a consistent user experience.\n\nNetwork Manager: Handles:\n-- Fetching conversation lists and message history\n-- Sending user prompts to the backend\n-- Receiving streamed responses from the server\n-- Managing auth headers and API tokens\n-- Tracking performance, errors, and user analytics\nState management is handled through a central store, using either React Context, Redux, or Zustand. \nThis global state holds conversation threads, user metadata, loading and error states, and UI preferences. \nIt enables any component to react to updates and keeps the UI in sync with the backend",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
