      "text": "* Chunked transfer encoding. For Express/Node.js, use res.write() and res.flush() to stream tokens to the client as soon as they’re available.\n* Token batching. Group tokens together (for example, send every 50 milliseconds) to reduce I/O overhead.\n* Backpressure control. Monitor the client’s buffer size. If the client is slow, pause token generation (for WebSocket) or skip writes.\n\n--- Latency Minimization\n* Edge functions. Use platforms like Vercel or Cloudflare Workers to reduce time-to-first-byte (TTFB).\n* Stream-start optimizations. Start emitting tokens as soon as the first token is ready. \nIf model latency is high, pre-fill the first token (using a fake-typing fallback).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "* Chunked transfer encoding. For Express/Node.js, use res.write() and res.flush() to stream tokens to the client as soon as they’re available.\n* Token batching. Group tokens together (for example, send every 50 milliseconds) to reduce I/O overhead.\n* Backpressure control. Monitor the client’s buffer size. If the client is slow, pause token generation (for WebSocket) or skip writes.\n\n--- Latency Minimization\n* Edge functions. Use platforms like Vercel or Cloudflare Workers to reduce time-to-first-byte (TTFB).\n* Stream-start optimizations. Start emitting tokens as soon as the first token is ready. \nIf model latency is high, pre-fill the first token (using a fake-typing fallback).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
